#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""gate-mission-scope — PreToolUse(Write|Edit|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit|Bash; Codex apply_patch): the
mission layer's role path guards (ROADMAP §4.12, "Role separation"; M9.9).

A builder never grades its own work, and a grader never builds:
  - a MISSION ROLE (market-researcher, product-tester, state-assessor, evaluator, mission-planner,
    ethics-reviewer) writes only its own paths (plugin/mission/roles.json `writes`) in the main tree,
    plus run data (.aladdin/, but not its logs/ or state/) and anything outside the project: never
    source, mission.json, another role's dir or a task worktree. It never commits, never runs the loop (`mission tick|cron|init`)
    and never runs a human's step (`mission approve`, `mission <area> approve|confirm|consent|veto|restore…`,
    `events authority`, `events emit`/`events decide` of a human event). Only the mission-planner creates
    Aladdin intents (`intent new`, `aladdin [run] "<intent>"`) or runs intake on one (`intent check|normalize`,
    which emit intake's intent.normalized): the others would skip the planner and the ethics review;
  - ANY OTHER DISPATCHED AGENT (a builder, an Aladdin planner) never writes docs/agents/mission/ in any
    tree (not through a Bash write, a tree removal or extract that reaches it, or a git pathspec), runs only
    the read-only `mission` commands (status, show, check, list, diff, due, --help: a bare area such as
    `mission evaluate` WRITES its report) and never emits a human event or intake's (intent.*);
  - NO MISSION ROLE OR BUILDER sets the judge command, ALOOP_JUDGE_CMD or ALOOP_JUDGE_TIMEOUT (an env
    prefix, env VAR=, export/declare/local/readonly, read/printf -v/mapfile/let into it, a nameref to it, or
    an assignment in a bash -c / interpreter string, where its `$` expansion counts too): a judge command a
    role picks could grade its own work (M9.42). Naming it as data (a grep pattern, a commit message) is
    no set. The supervisor may set it, and the evaluator runs `mission judge run`;
  - the SUPERVISOR (no agent_type) never hand-writes a role's artifact: everything under
    docs/agents/mission/ but mission.json (the human's, sealed by `mission approve`) is dispatched (only
    mkdir/touch may name the bare dir; a copy/extract/removal into or over it is a write of its contents,
    and so is a `git rm|mv` pathspec there, or a `git clean`/`git stash -u` that would take its untracked files);
  - NO ONE hand-writes docs/agents/mission/ledger.jsonl (only the mission CLI appends to it; a blocked write
    leaves it as it was, and a damage no gate saw is undone by the layout's own way, which the block names) or
    the captured prompts (<run data>/transcripts/, the UserPromptSubmit hook's), runs a hook's
    `transcripts prompt|record|…`, or, where a mission is set, starts a host session from a tool call
    (`claude -p`, `codex exec`, `opencode run`, `dsh <profile>`: its prompt would be captured as the human's
    words, which a grant reads, M9.17).

Write/Edit/patch paths are exact. A Bash command is read as the shell would read it (_shellread.py:
quotes, escapes, line continuations, comments, heredoc bodies as data, reserved words, subshells,
$(…) and `…` read as commands too), then judged per simple command: redirect targets; cp/mv/ln/
install/rsync destinations (and mv/rsync/zip -m sources, which are removed; mv -t too); rm/touch/
truncate/mkdir/tee files; sed -i, perl -i, awk -i and other in-place tools (sort -o, sponge, yq -i,
dos2unix, ed/ex/vim -c or +cmd) and formatters (ruff --fix|format, black, isort, prettier -w, gofmt -w,
eslint --fix, clang-format -i; not their check modes) inplace files (no path: the cwd, for ruff and
eslint); dd of=, curl -o/-O, wget (not --spider), find -delete and -exec/-execdir (CMD judged once per
start path, with {} a match under it and the text around {} kept), tar -x/--remove-files, unzip, zip,
patch, git merge-file; downloads and installs with a fixed output location (gh clone/fork/download, npm/
pnpm/yarn, pip, but not a global install); `cd`, `pushd` and `popd` followed (but a `cd` inside a
compound, group or pipeline element stays there); git writes in the project (a mission role's repo
writes, a builder's pathspecs into docs/agents/mission/ (with or without `--`, and through an ancestor
when they remove it or take another commit's files there), the supervisor's removals there, and the
commands of bisect run / rebase -x / submodule foreach); the `mission`, `events`, `intent` and `aladdin`
CLIs, also through `aloop|aladdin <tool>` (which exec that tool) and a package runner (npx, npm exec,
pnpm|yarn dlx, bunx). A removal (rm -r, find -delete, rsync --delete, a moved dir, git rm -r) of an
ancestor of docs/agents/mission/ is blocked: a tree's root counts (but not the supervisor's removal of
a task worktree), and find's -name tests bound it when every match must pass them (no -o, !, -not). An
extract into docs/agents/, where an archive's mission/ would land, is blocked too, and so is what is too
large to judge in linear time (FIND_WORK, CLIMB: a find's start paths × -exec words; GIT_ASKS). Wrappers (timeout,
env, nice, sudo, su, setsid, runuser, xargs, npx, stdbuf…) are looked through, and a shell string
(`bash -c`, `eval`, `env -S`, a heredoc or here-string fed to `bash` on stdin) or a script run by an
interpreter (`python3 …/bin/mission approve`) is read again. Variables set earlier in the command
resolve (incl. via export/declare/local and a `for`/`select` loop variable), and so do $PWD, $HOME,
the environment, $(pwd) and $(mktemp …) (a scratch dir outside the project). What only running it
would tell (a computed path) is judged by its known
directory, or not at all. A write made inside a program (`python3 -c …`) is invisible here:
gate-mission-artifact checks what changed in docs/agents/mission/ when the role stops.

Exit: 0 allow · 2 block (stderr, handed back to the model). Honors SKIP_HOOKS=1. Not an aloop project
(no docs/agents/) → allow. A crash once the call is ours to judge blocks (fail closed).
"""
import fnmatch
import json
import os
import posixpath
import re
import sys
import tempfile

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import _shellread as SR  # noqa: E402

GATE = "mission-scope"
EDIT_TOOLS = ("Write", "Edit", "MultiEdit", "NotebookEdit", "write", "edit")
SHELL_TOOLS = ("Bash", "bash", "shell")
PATCH_PATHS = re.compile(r"^\*\*\* (?:Add|Update|Delete) File: (.+)$|^\*\*\* Move to: (.+)$", re.M)
GIT_WRITES = {"commit", "push", "pull", "merge", "rebase", "cherry-pick", "am", "apply", "reset", "restore",
              "checkout", "switch", "stash", "rm", "mv", "add", "revert", "clean", "tag", "worktree", "notes",
              "update-ref", "branch", "config", "submodule", "sparse-checkout", "filter-branch", "replace",
